SUMMARY:SATURDAY NIGHT | Mama Said String Band
DESCRIPTION:Saturday\, July 25 | Taproom Stage | Doors: 7 pm | Show: 8 pm | $13.76 adv. Event Detail & Tickets \nMama Said String Band is an instant classic\, since 2016 they’ve been bringing their own brand of the grassroots music you’re so used to hearing to stages everywhere. Based out of Louisville\, KY\, Mama Said String Band brings a refreshing reinvention to Bluegrass\, Folk and Americana while focusing on vocal harmonies and contemporary instrumentation. \nHaving won several notable regional awards including album of the year in the Lexington Music Awards for “Carry The Water”\, Best Bluegrass Band in the Appalachian Arts and Entertainment Awards\, Bluegrass Artist of the Year in the Lexington Music Awards and with three nominations under their belt\, they have made a notable imprint in the Kentucky Music Scene. They bring big\, relatable emotions and honest songwriting to every show\, leaving fans always wanting more. \nFounded in 2005\, Pisgah is known for producing some of the most sought after craft ales in Western North Carolina. Pisgah Brewing Company currently operates the new indoor taproom with live music several days a week\, plus our outdoor music venue in the summer and fall months with live music frequently on WNC’s premier outdoor music venue\, the Pisgah Brewing Outdoor Stage. Bric’s Dip & Roll will be open Wednesday-Sunday from 4-10pm at the taproom! Be sure to come hungry\, thirsty and ready rock! Check out our upcoming schedule at pisgahbrewing.com/events
URL:https://livemusicasheville.com/calendar/mama-said-string-band/
LOCATION:Pisgah Brewing Company Black Mountain\, 2948 US-70\, Black Mountain\, NC\, 28711
CATEGORIES:Asheville Area,Black Mountain,Live Music
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://livemusicasheville.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/06/IMG_6002-e1784787000391.jpeg
GEO:35.6068069;-82.3568213
